Tensile (rocm-libraries, therock-7.14 / ROCm 7.14.0): enable non-HPA fp16
GEMM assembly kernels on gfx803 by running Tensile's fp16 codegen in an
unpacked "one fp16 per VGPR" mode, and fix the gfx803-only WGM work-group
division bug that made the resulting kernels silently miscompute.

WHY
---
gfx803 (Polaris) has no packed-fp16 hardware: all d16/d16_hi sub-dword
memory ops (buffer_load_short_d16_hi, ds_write_b16_d16_hi, ...),
v_pk_* packed fp16 ALU, and v_*_mix_f32 mixed-precision instructions are
GFX9+ only (confirmed against the live LLVM/AMDGPU assembler: every one
errors with "instruction not supported on this GPU (gfx803)"). Tensile's
fp16 kernels previously had no code path that could generate without
those instructions, so every fp16 GEMM on this hardware fell through to
the portability-only _fallback_ kernel. See
patches/rocblas/TENSILE_GFX803_FP16_TODO.md for the full investigation.

This patch has two parts:

1) HasD16 capability + halfNoD16 writer mode. Adds an AsmCaps capability
   `HasD16` (False on gfx803, runtime-probed via tryAssembler so it can't
   drift from reality), and a `halfNoD16` writer flag that selects
   unpacked fp16 codegen: buffer_load_ushort + in-place lshl/or packing in
   the global-read emitters, plain ds_write_b16 LDS stores (with
   v_lshrrev from the hi half for odd elements), scalar v_mul_f16 /
   v_add_f16 alpha/beta, per-element buffer_store_short stores and C beta
   loads, and an unpacked C-tile register layout. Also rewrites
   MAC_F16_Plain (upstream was silently broken: four identical
   v_mac_f16, op_sel dropped) to mirror FMA_F16_Packed's element mapping
   using SDWA src0_sel:WORD_1 selectors, which the RX 470 implements
   correctly (verified standalone).

2) gfx803 WGM division fix. After (1), the kernel generated, assembled and
   ran on the RX 470 but silently miscomputed: every thread's A loads
   collapsed to A[1..4] (B correct). Root cause: gfx803 lacks
   s_mul_hi_u32, so s_mul_int_64_32() falls back to computing the 64-bit
   scalar product in VECTOR registers (v0/v1). The WGM work-group
   division (graWorkGroup) runs that fallback and clobbers v0/v1, which
   hold the live GRO tile/unroll offsets (graTileAssignment) -- the
   init-code optimization (isInitCodeOptLW) emits that assignment before
   the kernel-arg-load wait, so those values are live when the WGM
   section runs. The tile-offset copy (v4=v0, v7=v1) then reads garbage,
   giving a uniform wrong GRO and the A[1..4] collapse. Fix: disable
   isInitCodeOptLW when HasSMulHi is False, so the tile assignment is
   emitted after the WGM section. On gfx900+ the same code is fine (the
   WGM division is pure scalar); the bug is latent upstream because
   gfx803 has been unsupported since ROCm 6.0.

REAL-HARDWARE VERIFICATION (RX 470, ROCm 7.14 client)
---
Kernel Cijk_Ailk_Bljk_H_MT32x64x8_SN_K1, client alpha=2 beta=0, after
this patch:
  - Exact [16,16,2,1]  (tail loop, M=16 edge):  0 validation mismatches
  - Exact [16,16,2,16] (unrolled main loop):     0 validation mismatches
  - Exact [32,64,8,1]: kernel D equals the expected 2*A*B element-for-
    element (0 mismatches vs expected); the client's own reference for
    that shape comes back sparse (a client-side reference issue for that
    problem shape, not the kernel -- every non-zero reference element
    matches the kernel).
The main-loop path uses the unchanged b64 loads; only the tail path's
u16+pack code is new. HPA (fp32-accumulate) fp16 remains impossible on
gfx803 (no v_pk_fma_f16/v_mad_mix_f32) -- this is non-HPA only, which is
what the fp16 GEMM needs here.

