FOLLOW-UP: gfx803-only asserts broke multi-arch (gfx803;gfx1010) Tensile
generation
---
Two of the hunks above were single-armed: they replaced the general
bpl==2-and-hi16 global-read code with the halfNoD16 (pre-Vega, unpacked f16)
sequence unconditionally, guarded only by `assert self.halfNoD16` instead of
an `if self.halfNoD16: ... else: <original code>` branch -- unlike the
sibling bpl==2-and-not-hi16 branches right next to them, which were patched
correctly (see the KernelWriterAssembly.py hunks below).

self.halfNoD16 is computed per kernel-writer instance from that kernel's own
target ISA (kernel["ISA"] -> self.asmCaps["HasD16"]), so it is already False
for any gfx9+/gfx10+ target -- gfx1010 (RDNA1) has real D16 hardware, so
self.halfNoD16 is correctly False there. The bug was never that gfx1010
kernels were misidentified as gfx803; it is that reaching this chooseGlobalRead
branch AT ALL (bpl==2, hi16, whatever the ISA) was mistaken for proof of being
on gfx803. Any fp16 GEMM kernel generated for gfx1010, gfx900, or any other
HasD16 architecture that happens to take this global-read shape hits
`assert self.halfNoD16` and aborts Tensile's kernel generation -- which is
exactly what surfaced once this repo started building gfx803;gfx1010 in one
Tensile run instead of gfx803 alone.

Fix: give both `bpl==2 and hi16` branches (BufferLoad and flat/global) the
same `if self.halfNoD16: <no-d16 sequence> \n <original d16_hi instruction>`
shape their `not hi16` siblings already had, so the original
_buffer_load_d16_hi_b16 / _global_load_d16_hi_b16 codegen is restored for
every HasD16 architecture, gfx1010 included, and the no-d16 sequence still
only runs when self.halfNoD16 is actually true.

Verified: applied to a fresh checkout of shared/tensile at this repo's pinned
ROCM_LIBRARIES_REF (release/therock-10.0) with `patch -p1`, applies cleanly
with no fuzz, `assert self.halfNoD16` no longer appears anywhere in
KernelWriterAssembly.py, and the patched file passes `python3 -m py_compile`.
Not yet re-verified on real gfx1010 hardware -- re-run the RX 470 gfx803
validation in the original REAL-HARDWARE VERIFICATION section above too,
since the same file changed.

